# docs/.gitignore — a WORKING DOCUMENT keeps no PDF.
#
# A division ledger is a WORKING DOCUMENT: append-only, read in the editor by the division that
# writes it, restamped by `node engine/status.js --write`, and never handed to anyone as a document.
# The deliverables — white paper, deck, technical docs, SUMMARY — keep their PDFs and are unaffected.
#
# THE MEASURED REASON (2026-09-06, docs/_reports/2026-09-06-repo-cleanup.md):
# the five ledger PDFs are 132.4 MB of a 524 MB pack, 25% of this repository's whole history, and
# docs/ENGINE.pdf alone is 108.4 MB across ten rebuilds — the single largest object class here.
# PDFs do not delta-compress, so each rebuild pays close to full price again: 16.6 MB of pack per
# pass over the five, 13.9 MB of it ENGINE.
#
# THE SAVING IS ENTIRELY FUTURE. Untracking these recovers ZERO bytes of existing history — the
# blobs stay in the pack and only a history rewrite removes them, which this project has ruled out
# (271 commit hashes resolve in tracked markdown today, and figures are traced back to runs by hash).
#
# This lives here rather than in the root .gitignore so that the ledger rule sits beside the ledgers.
# build/build_pdfs.js derives the same set from .claude/agents/*.md and prints it on every run; if
# a sixth division appears, add its ledger PDF here too.
ENGINE.pdf
MEASURE.pdf
SEARCH.pdf
OPS.pdf
WEB.pdf

# THE RULE IS THE WORKING DOCUMENT, NOT THE LEDGER — 2026-09-06, second pass.
# A ledger is one KIND of working document. Two more were left in on the day the rule landed, and
# build/build_pdfs.js now carries them as a DECLARED RESIDUAL with a reason each, because the shared
# property could not be derived — five candidate derivations were measured over all 78 docs/*.md and
# every one over- or under-matched; they are listed in that file's header.
#
# ROADMAP.md is the register, read as gate input by open_work / quarantine / register_reality /
# seed_source_audit, and it moves most sessions. MEASURED: docs/ROADMAP.pdf is 7,229,637 B in the
# tree across EIGHT tracked versions holding 16.42 MB raw / 5.19 MB packed, and the version at the
# most recent bump d7ed4b75 packs to 4,092,583 B — 4.09 MB of permanent history per rebuild.
#
# RUNNING-NOTES.md gains a row every change by design (.githooks/pre-commit blocks a commit that
# does not move it). Its PDF has never been built; priced once to a scratch path it is 241,109 B
# TODAY at 190 lines, and docs/ENGINE.pdf at 108.4 MB is what that number becomes.
#
# UNTRACKING RECOVERS ZERO BYTES OF EXISTING HISTORY, here as above. build/build_pdfs.js THROWS if
# an excluded document's PDF is still tracked, so this file and that one cannot drift apart quietly.
ROADMAP.pdf
RUNNING-NOTES.pdf
